# Post-Change Test & Verify (Required)

When finishing work that changed **backend/** or **frontend/** source or config, do the following. Do not skip.

**When this applies**: After any change to backend/frontend source or config; before considering a task "done". Triggers: code change, feature complete, error fix, before verify. See also: `run-tests.md`, `verify.md`, `.cursor/skills/test-workflow/SKILL.md`.

## Delegation (Step 5 → QA)

When the work was done via **subagent delegation** (e.g. Frontend/Backend/DB subagent implemented per a requirement doc), **do not run verification or update §5 in the main chat**. Instead:

- **Delegate Step 5 to the QA subagent**: Instruct the user to switch to the **QA** subagent and pass: (1) the requirement doc (at least §3 test approach), (2) confirmation that **build and restart are done**. QA runs verification per `.cursor/commands/verify.md` and updates §5 (and §6 for error fixes). After QA completes, the main agent may **commit** per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`.
- **Exception**: If the user said "code only here", "skip subagent", or "do it in this chat", the main agent performs sections 1–4 below (run tests, verify, §5, commit).

Reference: `docs/workflow/SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md` (Step 5 → QA).

## 1. Unit tests

- **Backend changed**: Run `cd backend && mvn test`. Fix failures and re-run.
- **Frontend changed**: Run `cd frontend && npm test -- --watchAll=false`. Fix failures and re-run.
- **Both**: Run both. Record result (pass/fail, summary) in the requirement doc **§5 Test results**.

## 2. Verification (restart and health check)

- Read `.cursor/commands/verify.md` and follow its restart and check steps. For shortcuts: `.cursor/commands/restart-all.md`, `check-backend.md`, `check-frontend-backend.md`.
- Restart: `./scripts/dev-services.sh {frontend|backend|all} restart` per scope. Wait 5–10s after backend restart.
- **Health check**: Backend 9200 `curl -s http://localhost:9200/api/health` → 200 + JSON; frontend 3001 `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:3001` → 2xx; if DB used, `curl -s http://localhost:9200/api/db/test` → `data.connected === true`.

## 3. On failure

- Create **bugfix child requirement**: `docs/requirements/{parentID}-bugfix-{N}.md` (template: `docs/template/BUGFIX_CHILD_TEMPLATE.md`). Fix per that doc, then repeat from step 1 until all pass.

## 4. On success

- Update requirement doc §5 and checklist. For error/bug fixes add **§6 Error remedy result**.
- **Commit** the changes per `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md` (do not push unless the user requests).

See: `.cursor/commands/verify.md`, `.cursor/commands/commit-on-complete.md`, `run-tests.md`, `docs/workflow/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md`, `WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md`, `docs/workflow/SUBAGENT-DELEGATION.md`, `docs/workflow/WHY-TESTS-VERIFY-NOT-AUTO.md`.
